# R23 the summit of Rowan's Rise: the Wicker Man, the Crooked Man's end, Phillip in the ash, the road home. By hand, polished by Gemini, unvoiced.

~ arrive
Narrator: A spiral of small stones is laid on the crown of the hill, with stone-lined rays running out of it and ten bonfires round the edge on scorched rust-red earth.
Narrator: At its heart stands the Wicker Man, sixty feet of woven willow bound with wire and iron, and in the cages of its chest and limbs, people are praying.
set wv_summit_seen
quest wickers_vigil shadow_of_the_wicker_man
-> END

~ effigy
Narrator: Through the weave of the chest cage you can see a woman's calm face among villagers, goats and sheep. A single tear has run down her cheek, and she is looking at nothing.
crooked_man [sly]: Look at her, my darlings. Ladies and gentlemen, the last piece! She is not even afraid. Do you not love that in a person?
-> effigy_menu

~ effigy_menu
* Call to Adela -> adela
* Ask the Crooked Man why -> why
* [if item:wv_barnaby_repellent and not flag.wv_repellent_used] Spray Barnaby's Wicker Man Repellent -> repellent
* Tell him to let them go -> demand
* Light the fire and begin -> begin
* Not yet -> END

~ adela
Narrator: Adela's eyes meet yours through the weave. She does not speak. Nothing you can cast, throw or shout reaches her. She shakes her head, once, gently, like someone declining an offer.
-> effigy_menu

~ why
crooked_man [sly]: Why? Because she is the sacrifice, and I am the host. Because the Queen asked me to, and I am very good at being asked. Because it is going to be a splendid fire.
-> effigy_menu

~ repellent
Narrator: You spray Barnaby's repellent across the weave. A small cloud of vinegar rises, and the wicker, which is made of willow, does not seem to care. A very long silence follows.
crooked_man [sly]: Oh, I like that one.
set wv_repellent_used
take wv_barnaby_repellent
-> effigy_menu

~ demand
crooked_man [angry]: Let them go? The one thing I have never done in my life.
-> effigy_menu

~ begin
cutscene wv_final_sacrifice
Narrator: Flames climb the effigy while masked dancers caper in the firelight, and the ground trembles with their hymn.
cutscene wv_final_sacrifice_2
Narrator: Behind the weave, Adela's eye, and a single tear. The flames come up past it. The cut is clean.
cutscene wv_final_sacrifice_3
Narrator: The titan lurches one step forward, and its eyes catch fire.
cutscene end
set wv_wicker_lit
combat wv_wicker_man

~ crooked_end
cutscene wv_crooked_mans_end
Narrator: The Wicker Man comes apart in a column of sparks that goes up past the moon, and the whole hill is lit orange for a breath.
cutscene wv_crooked_mans_end_2
Narrator: In the ash, something small and shrivelled and crooked claws its way out of a heap of embers. It is blackened to the bone and still wearing its grin.
crooked_man [angry]: My queen. My Queen! You said I would be at your right hand. I did every single thing you asked. I did it all so well. Why have you...
cutscene wv_crooked_mans_end_3
Narrator: He falls still. Rain begins on the smoking ash.
cutscene end
set wv_crooked_end_seen
set crooked_man_destroyed
quest wickers_vigil the_ash
-> END

~ phillip_ash
cutscene wv_phillip_in_ash
Narrator: A man in a ruined coat comes up the hill at a stumble, burned and out of breath, with a name in his mouth that he keeps shouting. He gets to the ash, and stops.
phillip_druskenvald [sad]: Adela.
cutscene wv_phillip_in_ash_2
Narrator: He kneels in the ash. He puts his hands into it. When he lifts them out there is a blackened necklace in one, with a planchette on it.
phillip_druskenvald [sad]: She was waiting for me. She was waiting for me the whole time, and I was in the wrong place.
cutscene end
-> phillip_menu

~ phillip_menu
* Ask if he is hurt -> phillip_hurt
* Tell him she could not be saved -> phillip_saved
* Offer to help him bury her -> phillip_bury
* Let him be -> phillip_go

~ phillip_hurt
phillip_druskenvald [weary]: Does it matter? The wisps took me up the wrong hill. I fell in a stream. I do not know what I did. I only know where I was not.
-> phillip_menu

~ phillip_saved
phillip_druskenvald [sad]: I knew. I think I always did. It does not make it any easier to carry.
-> phillip_menu

~ phillip_bury
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: No. Thank you, but no. I will do it myself. I should have done everything myself.
-> phillip_menu

~ phillip_go
Narrator: He wraps the bones in his coat, and he goes down the hill without another word. He does not seem to see the village, the fire or you.
set wv_phillip_seen
-> END

~ rowan
Narrator: A flat stone at the spiral's centre, carved with a woman's name and an antlered hare. The legend says Rowan climbed to sit on the moon. The stones say otherwise. They say she was the first one burned here.
-> END

~ fall_back
Narrator: The way back down is open. The village is far behind you, and what is chained in the cages above you cannot wait.
-> vigil/square:retreat_confirm

~ home
Narrator: You take the road down from the hill, through a night that smells of wet ash. Behind you the bonfires burn low one by one. The moon is still too big, and still grinning.
set wicker_man_burned
quest wickers_vigil ashes_to_ashes
xp milestone
move wickermoor_village
